{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/724778-scion-in-wod-2nd-ed-homebrew","id":724778,"title":"Scion in WoD 2nd Ed Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-24T19:27:01-07:00","id":724778,"title":"Scion in WoD 2nd Ed Homebrew","content":"So first of all it's been ages since I played Scion so please go easy on me for any misconceptions I may have about the old mechanics/setting.<br /> <br /> But I had an idea for a game I wanted to run and it pretty much had to be in the Scion universe, but I'm loving God Machine/ nWoD 2nd Ed rules right now so I'm going to attempt a port of old Scion into that system with simplified rules. I'd appreciate suggestions and constructive criticisms on my mechanics from some people who know the old system better than I do.<br /> <br /> So basically here's what I got:<br /> 1) the core is nWoD 2nd Ed with a supernatural template.<br /> 2) Legend is the &quot;core&quot; supernatural stat limiting magical power advancement (similar to Blood Potency or Primal Urge, I'm sure there's a term for these) with scions gaining temporary dots of &quot;fate&quot; that they can spend on powers based on legend. Legend increases when dramatically appropriate and cannot be raised with XP.<br /> 3) legendary attributes still award one automatic success when rolling that attribute, but Domains now follow the rules for Influences in Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd ed on page 186.<br /> 4) at character generation Scions gain five supernatural powers which can be distributed as dots between legendary attributes and domains.<br /> ...(a) one dot must be associated with the Scion's mythic parent and one must be associated with their pantheon.<br /> ...(b) there is a limit to the total dots of mythic traits a Scion my have based on Legend, identical to attribute caps based on Spirit rank in W:tF2e<br /> ...(c) titanspawn characters have no pantheon but must take two powers associated with their parent<br /> 5) both legendary attributes and domains now have associated knacks<br /> ...(a) when increasing a legendary attribute or domain scions gain one free knack associated with that attribute or domain.<br /> ...(b) domain knacks allow for a variety of effects but the domains of 1st edition would make good examples.<br /> ...(c) additional knacks may be purchased for any domain or legendary attribute the scion possesses for four XP after character creation.<br /> <br /> ... And that's about it. Trying to keep it simple for now.<br /> <br /> For those unfamiliar with W:tF2e spirits generally have influence dots equal to their rank which allow them to control, strengthen and create things associated with the influence's type. Small changes can be affected with only one dot but for bigger or longer lasting or more precise affects spirits require more dots of influence based on a simple table in the Werewolf book. It's pretty free-form. It'll cost a point of fate for scions and for now I'm going to allow my players the option to dump all their points into legendary attributes or domains as they see fit to maximize character options.<br /> <br /> Knacks will require a lot of work but for now I've given myself these guidelines:<br /> A knack may,<br /> 1) add one bonus die when rolling a type of action with that domain or attribute (ex: +1 die to all damage using the fire domain)<br /> 2) add one automatic success to actions of a certain type rolled on/against a specific target (ex: +1 success when damaging the undead with the fire domain)<br /> 3) grant a unique permanent boon of lesser power (ex: +1 natural soak per dot of legendary stamina)<br /> 4) waive the fate cost for a specific use of a known domain (ex: granting fire breath as an innate ability)<br /> or 5) make a specific action rote when rolled with that attribute and spending a fate point (ex: when rolling Intelligence + Computers with legendary intelligence)<br /> <br /> So far these are my mechanical edits. Any suggestions on what I can add? Problems people see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 10-24-2015, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T19:57:57-07:00","id":724863,"title":"","content":"Some years ago i toyed along with some other people in the H:tV forum about a pervasiveness in Task Force: Valkyrie of terms and imagery taken from norse mythology that went a little beyond tongue-in-cheek geekery - Hod rounds being a specially egregious case - and leading to ramblings about the secret supporters behind the conspiracy being <b>exactly</b> what says in the tin: the choosers of the slain, making a fraternity of warriors, tricksters and geniuses raising arms against the forces of the dark and chaos. A gathering of the dutiful and brave marked for an unending war against supernatural terrors that would cost the lives of most.<br /> <br /> A collection of heroes, to serve in death in a battle greater than any of their mortal lives. Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> And from there it basically snowballed into porting Scion: Ragnarok into nWoD, using the Dark Heroes from Mirrors as expies for Heroes &amp; Demigods, with a bit of the Purified (from Immortals) added in to portray the Aesir and Vanir. Fun stuff indeed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:01:12-07:00","id":726178,"title":"","content":"Looks like a pretty solid base so far. Could also see modeling Domain Knacks off of Spirit Numina to cut down a bit of the work there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}